text.section:
In executing its duties under this chapter, the Board shall:

Foster, encourage, and promote the safe and efficient exploration for and development, production, and conservation of gas and oil resources located in the Commonwealth;


Administer a method of gas and oil conservation for the purpose of maximizing exploration, development, production, and utilization of gas and oil resources;


Administer procedures for the recognition and protection of the rights of gas or oil owners with interests in gas or oil resources contained within a pool;


Promote the maximum production and recovery of coal without substantially affecting the right of a gas owner proposing a gas well to explore for and produce gas; and


Hear and decide appeals of the Director's decisions and orders issued under Article 3 (§ 45.2-1629 et seq.).
